The scalp surface mesh embedded in the baked field maps under `src/config/topography/` — vertex positions, normals,
triangles and ambient occlusion — derives from the head surface of the fsaverage average subject,
`fsaverage-head.fif`, which is distributed inside the mne package and originates with FreeSurfer.

That mesh is a modified version of the original FreeSurfer surface, and is marked as such here so it is not
mistaken for the original: vertices below z = -0.06 m in MNE head coordinates are dropped and the triangles
re-indexed onto what remains, and a per-vertex ambient occlusion term that the original does not carry is computed
and stored with it. `tools/topography/bake_fieldmap.py` is what performs both modifications.

